    "case_id": "738",
    "case_summary": "An 11-month-old male child developed fever one week after receiving the measles vaccine. The fever initially resolved with Cefuroxime Axetil Granules within 2-3 days but recurred for about 10 days. After three months, the child was admitted due to increased fever frequency and decreased fever relief time to 8-12 hours. Past medical history includes pneumonia, duodenal bulb ulcer, erosive gastritis, and surgical treatment three years ago for Staphylococcus aureus septicemia and infective endocarditis.\n\nInitial examination showed:- Congestion of the pharynx- Grade 1 swelling of both tonsils- Coarse breath sounds in both lungsOn second admission:- Liver palpable 4 cm below rib margin- Tenderness on liver percussion\n\nLaboratory Tests:- Initial WBC: 20.2×10^9/L- CRP: 146.4mg/L- Procalcitonin: 0.69ng/mL- ESR: 120mm/h- Blood film: rare neutrophilsImaging Studies:1. Abdominal CT:- Title: Plain and enhanced CT scan of upper abdomen- Description: Patchy, slightly low-density shadow in segment IV of liver, measuring 5.3x3.4x3.9cm. Abnormal perfusion of liver parenchyma around lesion in arterial phase. Honeycomb enhancement in delayed phase.2. Abdominal MRI:- Title: Abdominal MRI of liver lesion- Description: Mass shadow with mixed signal in SIV segment of liver, measuring 55mm × 42mm × 64mm. Honeycomb-like enhancement with narrow-band edema signals.Genetic Testing:- Heterozygous mutation in exon 3 of the ELANE genePathology:- Liver tissue showed scattered hepatic structures with focal abscess changes- Culture from liver lesion: Positive for Staphylococcus aureus",
